00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.360
coming out of it.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.940
Who did the artistry on the
skin, 'cause the air brushing,

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:08.310
however it's printed, airbrushed...
how do you do it?

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:10.720
- Yeah, it's actually silicone paint

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.190
and our creative guy, Mike,
painted your whole skin.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:19.700
And then each one of those
hairs, is a human hair,

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:24.140
and each one is individually
punched one by one by hand.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.770
- Good grief. That is...

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:27.910
- Yes.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.560
- I think more so for me.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:30.393
- Yes.

00:05:30.393 --> 00:05:32.380
- Because I, like this is
not looking into the mirror,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.420
this is looking into a very weird mirror.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.360
- Yes, exactly.
When you look into a mirror,

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.870
you see a mirrored image of yourself.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.410
This is not a mirrored image,
this is the other way.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.243
- Oh! It is.

00:05:41.243 --> 00:05:42.710
- It's always going to look
even more weird to you.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:43.960
- Yeah.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.120
It just did a thing,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.270
